%description:

Tcp.notsentLowat:off -- no low-water mark: the application gets no send-ready indication.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "-1B: off".

The classes: off (-1B, the default), mark (0B and more), and socket-override: a
TCP_NOTSENT_LOWAT of the socket takes the place of the parameter. The code: the indication
TCP_I_SEND_MSG when the unsent bytes fall to the mark (TcpConnection::sendData()), and the
socket option in initConnection(). This test separates "off" from "mark".

Host under test: host1, whose application writes 100000 bytes after the handshake.
Observation: level 1 at the application: no socketSendReady (TCP_I_SEND_MSG) in 3 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.notsentLowat
%# class: off
%# value: -1B
%# key: *.host1.tcp.notsentLowat
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpNotsentLowatOff")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.app[0]").signal("socketEstablished").within(0.1))
        .act(action().after(0.001).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 100000);
        }))
        .never(on("host1.app[0]").signal("socketSendReady")
              .describe("a send-ready indication")
              .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpNotsentLowatOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.notsentLowat = -1B    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpNotsentLowatOff: PASS
